      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "n8n-style-automation-template"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Sketch, Not Confirmed\n\nThis graph is first-pass reasoning from one line — \"create a brainstorm graph about an n8n-style template for Twilite\" — grounded in how n8n actually works (trigger/action/branch nodes, typed item-carrying connections), not a validated design.\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Modeled or executable? (see the open Question node — this decides almost everything else)\n- Does existing script/task machinery actually suffice to run a workflow, or is a real execution engine needed? (see the contested Assumption node)\n- Design-surface-only, with execution staying external, is a real, much smaller alternative (see the Alternative node) worth deciding against deliberately, not defaulting into."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "portId": "guided-by",
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
