      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Design Surface Only, Execution Stays External",
        "description": "Twilite graphs represent the workflow visually and structurally — triggers, actions, branches, data shape — but an external runtime (n8n itself, a serverless function, some other executor) actually runs it, reading the graph as its definition rather than Twilite executing anything.",
        "tradeoffs": "Much smaller scope: no execution engine, no credential storage, no run history to build — but the automation still depends on something outside Twilite to actually do anything, which only partly solves the original problem (design lives in Twilite, execution still doesn’t).",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "n8n-style-automation-template"
        },
        "presentation": {
